# Diagnosis ladder 1/3 (2026-10-25): LQR alone (VAR47=12), xy steps instead of the figure-8.
# Question: how lightly damped is the closed xy loop, and does an x move pull y (coupling)?
# Each goto is a short ramped move (default motion), then a 5 s dwell: overshoot and ringing in the dwell give the
# damping; y motion during the x steps (and x during y) gives the coupling. Same exp row and sets as
# lab_e_exp_lqr_u0_d12.fly, so it compares 1:1 with that flight. UNVERIFIED: never flown.
campaign lab-e-diag-lqr-steps
rate 100
log velocity_loops camera_fusion
slow 50 nn4 xy_ctrl mrac_3l mrac_theta ekf_states estimator_truth thrust_model optical_flow takeoff_gate mrac_shadow
exp lqr_3l
set g_traj_ff_shift_s=0 g_land_xy_gate_cm=10 g_xyc_delay_ticks=12
takeoff 0.5 mrac_injection=0
hold 3
goto x=0.3 y=0 z=0.5 dwell_s=5
hold 5
goto x=0 y=0.3 z=0.5 dwell_s=5
hold 5
land
